      "nets": ["+5V", "GND", "RST", "SCK", "SDA", "PWM", "POT", "TACH"],
      "observed": "The netlist contains two MCU footprints connected in parallel: U2 is ATtiny45-20P (DIP-8) and U3 is ATtiny13V-10S (SOIC-8W). U3 shares every MCU net with U2: VCC to +5V, GND to GND, reset to RST, I2C pins to SDA/SCK, analog input to POT, tach input to TACH, and PWM/MISO to PWM. There is no DNP or selection indication in the netlist.",
      "expected": "The specification describes the board as 'an ATtiny-driven fan controller' (singular). If the board is intended to have a single ATtiny, only one MCU should be populated/represented. If dual footprints are intentional, only one should be populated or the other should be clearly non-populated; additionally, an ATtiny13V part should not be powered from the +5V rail if its rating is low-voltage.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"U3\")\n      (value \"ATtiny13V-10S\")\n      (footprint \"Package_SO:SOIC-8W_5.3x5.3mm_P1.27mm\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If both MCU footprints are populated, their push-pull outputs can contend, especially on PWM/PB1, and the board may draw excess current, behave unpredictably, or damage one or both MCUs. U3 being an ATtiny13V part on the +5V rail is also questionable if that variant is low-voltage.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show an extra ATtiny MCU footprint (U3) wired in parallel with the intended single ATtiny controller (U2), which is a likely deviation from the intended fan-controller design and can cause bus/output contention or voltage-rating issues."
}

